-- title:
--   Residue structure at a ramified prime of a maximal order
-- statement:
--   Let $q\neq q'$ be primes, let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $B=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra, assumed to satisfy `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: either $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb Q$ the completed algebra $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb Q$ and is finitely generated, and every order containing $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $\mu\in\Lambda$ satisfy $\mu^{2}=-qq'$, and let $\star:\Lambda\to\Lambda$ be any map with $\mu\,x^{\star}=\bar x\,\mu$ for all $x\in\Lambda$, where $\bar{\phantom{x}}$ is quaternionic conjugation. Let $p$ be a prime with $p=q$ or $p=q'$. Then there exist $\omega\in\Lambda$ and $t,n\in\mathbb Z$ such that: $\omega+\bar\omega=t$ and $\omega\bar\omega=n$ in $B$; the polynomial $X^{2}-tX+n$ has no root in $\mathbb Z/p$; $t^{2}-4n\neq 0$ in $\mathbb Z/p$; $\mu\omega+\omega\mu-t\mu=p\,z$ for some $z\in\Lambda$ (equivalently $\mu\omega-\bar\omega\mu\in p\Lambda$); $\omega^{\star}-\omega=\mu(c_{0}+c_{1}\omega)+p\,y$ for some $c_{0},c_{1}\in\mathbb Z$ and $y\in\Lambda$; $\omega^{\star}=\omega+p\,l_{1}+\mu\,l_{2}$ for some $l_{1},l_{2}\in\Lambda$; $\mu^{\star}=-\mu$; $\star$ is involutive on $\Lambda$; and $1^{\star}=1$.
--
--   This packages the local structure at a prime of ramification of an indefinite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb Q$ ramified exactly at $q$ and $q'$: locally at $p$ the maximal order is generated by the unramified quadratic extension together with a uniformiser, and $\omega$ is an element whose reduction generates the residue field $\mathbb F_{p^{2}}$, with $\mu$ playing the role of the uniformiser intertwining $\omega$ with its Frobenius twist. It serves as the arithmetic input, used through [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialModule.eq_zero_of_forall_apply_apply_eq_apply_star_apply_of_forall_apply_self_eq_zero_of_trace_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialModule.eq_zero_of_forall_apply_apply_eq_apply_star_apply_of_forall_apply_self_eq_zero_of_trace_eq), for the analysis of special modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the relevant Shimura curve.
